      "side": 1,
      "message": "`lvl1_sz \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c order) \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT` is the L1 table size in **bytes**, but `lvl1_idx` is an **entry** index, and a two-level table\u0027s L1 entry is architecturally fixed at 8 bytes. So `lvl1_idx \u003e\u003d lvl1_sz` permits an index up to ~8x the valid count, and `host_table[lvl1_idx]` / `hyp_table[lvl1_idx] \u003d ...` then read/write out of bounds of the L1 table in EL2. `id` here is the host-supplied Device ID from MAPD. How about `if (lvl1_idx \u003e\u003d lvl1_sz / sizeof(u64))`?",
